{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And after my skin they have surrounded this</b> — like <i>and the thickets of the forest shall be cut down</i> [Isaiah 10:34]. The meaning of <b>זאת</b> is \"my self,\" <b>ועורי ובשרי</b> being appositional." "<b>I would see El</b> — the afflictions that He renews upon me."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra parses ואחר עורי נקפו זאת against the received vocalization (נִקֵּפוּ as Qal 3mp); he reads זאת as 'this [thing],' i.e., the speaker himself, with the following words in apposition. The comparison is to the root נקף 'to cut/shear.'", 1 "He reads אחזה as conditional/optative: 'I would see El' in the very afflictions He brings. The referent of 'the afflictions' is supplied from context, not stated explicitly in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:07.427448105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}